[{:db/id "q-345206/field-1/2827df713ae25968ff49215651b41e52882642731db05ccf3bb62771162a8a6e" :answer/id #uuid "92aff546-a8cf-506e-8cda-2773ca87f447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{t^2+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345206/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c72c1987-ec25-54f4-8b2c-27a961d701fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345206/field-1/2827df713ae25968ff49215651b41e52882642731db05ccf3bb62771162a8a6e" :answer-field/choices ["q-345206/field-1/2827df713ae25968ff49215651b41e52882642731db05ccf3bb62771162a8a6e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345206" :question/id #uuid "45eb9b77-c6ce-5aa4-801c-a93678ce677f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345206" :question/problem "A body of mass $1\\,\\text{kg}$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)$ meters per second.  Find an expression for the force acting on the particle at time $t.$\n\n$F(t)=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345206/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345206"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345207/field-1/cb3e135b39bf62662b725b1ed7e1c3060cc935e7cd5bb0e91fc9115ecbb9c166" :answer/id #uuid "8dfd070b-2a61-59f4-92b6-41c47413e794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8t}{\\sqrt{1-t^2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345207/field-1/5b47c6d100bf8c7b0112f49d46a93ca4da89c41bbad30e5ccebfc739d611ba4a" :answer/id #uuid "6be53d43-1d90-5c86-99f5-e9726f77f703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345207/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f36f7e29-def4-5e9b-b019-e4536d1d2707" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345207/field-1/cb3e135b39bf62662b725b1ed7e1c3060cc935e7cd5bb0e91fc9115ecbb9c166" :answer-field/choices ["q-345207/field-1/cb3e135b39bf62662b725b1ed7e1c3060cc935e7cd5bb0e91fc9115ecbb9c166" "q-345207/field-1/5b47c6d100bf8c7b0112f49d46a93ca4da89c41bbad30e5ccebfc739d611ba4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345207" :question/id #uuid "e8a625fd-0a7f-5970-a294-68b09e11cf6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345207" :question/problem "A body of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=t\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)$ meters per second.  Find an expression for the force acting on the particle at time $t.$\n\n$F(t)=8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)\\,+$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)+t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)+t\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(t)+\\frac{8t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345207/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345207"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889/selection/c7df3d30f90a7df668325ad06d6f681edfaf4ac22f83ec79f44f5240231be1e4" :answer/id #uuid "3c1fc86d-1ed1-5f78-aca6-a90bfedecf2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889/selection/cc711e6f789fbc6775f97cfdf12568624da2841f5947b4aa7ab64b7331fa39fc" :answer/id #uuid "75e68ff6-a34e-58e9-9f7c-c4882bcd1618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889/selection/0288fd2da33bf8942d1b5feb1dba9b8a6744a53d92a9a45330cef8cc5baca740" :answer/id #uuid "f9d5b3d4-64c0-5d57-817a-4225cbe120b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889/selection/85732c6d8b20455b883784c01b47cde501586949dfbdafdd65e2637fc9294ebf" :answer/id #uuid "efa19a68-6b95-5060-b453-8623e1560f27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889/selection/ed2bea73019d750a65b2194297cd47b5b468796305ce4f17ef66f281924f0306" :answer/id #uuid "dcb21bf7-89ea-5846-a793-743ffe5ebf58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0abc5fc0-d2da-5fa8-8173-bde814c17f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138889/selection/cc711e6f789fbc6775f97cfdf12568624da2841f5947b4aa7ab64b7331fa39fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-138889/selection/c7df3d30f90a7df668325ad06d6f681edfaf4ac22f83ec79f44f5240231be1e4" "q-138889/selection/cc711e6f789fbc6775f97cfdf12568624da2841f5947b4aa7ab64b7331fa39fc" "q-138889/selection/0288fd2da33bf8942d1b5feb1dba9b8a6744a53d92a9a45330cef8cc5baca740" "q-138889/selection/85732c6d8b20455b883784c01b47cde501586949dfbdafdd65e2637fc9294ebf" "q-138889/selection/ed2bea73019d750a65b2194297cd47b5b468796305ce4f17ef66f281924f0306"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138889" :question/id #uuid "8c20835d-7bd8-5e9c-8ea5-8bdbf915a1be" :question/math-academy-id "q-138889" :question/problem "A body of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=4\\sqrt{t}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-3)$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=4$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}-\\frac{5}{t-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}}-\\frac{5}{4-3} \\\\  & =1-5 \\\\  & =-4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F|=|-32|=32\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138889/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138889"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345227/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c09c9dd6-4afc-5e75-89df-a1fb2517f727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345227/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9c9172c6-2360-508f-8ace-832111819474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345227/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "761a5017-d38e-51fc-b9c8-f7283907b94a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345227/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-345227/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-345227/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345227" :question/id #uuid "1f09fa8f-3853-500b-aee6-60e0f296f95d" :question/math-academy-id "q-345227" :question/problem "A body of mass $\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=4{e}^{\\frac{t}{2}}$ meters per second. \n\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ seconds. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the force equals\n{{field-1}} $\\text{N}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{e}^{\\frac{t}{2}}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{\\frac{t}{2}}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{\\frac{t}{2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\frac{t}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =2{e}^{\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =2(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =ma(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)|=|1|=1\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345227/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345227"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-315648/field-1/c1965dae7f538d08f8234cfba7b72c0f0ad0e70890bd34332f833aebc976a57d" :answer/id #uuid "e143678e-4dfa-51c9-bd27-7dbfe99013c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16t+12\\cos(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315648/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e4b3527-f8b3-54b0-a13c-75d3e73ae462" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315648/field-1/c1965dae7f538d08f8234cfba7b72c0f0ad0e70890bd34332f833aebc976a57d" :answer-field/choices ["q-315648/field-1/c1965dae7f538d08f8234cfba7b72c0f0ad0e70890bd34332f833aebc976a57d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315648" :question/id #uuid "23bec17b-f4e5-5238-be97-5731032f5907" :question/math-academy-id "q-315648" :question/problem "A body of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=2{t}^{2}+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ meters per second.  Find an expression for the force acting on the particle at time $t.$\n\n$F(t)=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =4t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (4t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =16t+12\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-315648/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-315648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345339/field-1/110aa16e0017d43b3ce6185ae160f6d1e87b8b6cf6ff3b8b8b4a7fd5e92085c3" :answer/id #uuid "e678ad20-8680-52b6-9bc9-38874c470ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cos(t)+t\\sin(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186310715 :answer-field/choices ["q-345339/field-1/110aa16e0017d43b3ce6185ae160f6d1e87b8b6cf6ff3b8b8b4a7fd5e92085c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900/selection/0e60425cd3a5ff39671f252f602bfefa18c9c7a468398112ec2fa0ffa1233932" :answer/id #uuid "40a6fefa-fb2e-550e-8275-b40a631dd214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24{t}^{2}-12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900/selection/83f429aa058db522ffedd829be8affa7ea9b01582aac18fc5d93a2a476fd4615" :answer/id #uuid "4c5132e9-fe86-5b0e-8ba3-3e73526ccf9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{t}^{2}+12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900/selection/3a4cb68b6e2420440de2a5cf842cef8eda752c3a9743289f13ed7cf2875628e2" :answer/id #uuid "ed574d9a-666c-561a-88d5-73583042eff1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{t}^{2}-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900/selection/6cd854ef01bc12a8d9afee61c004093a65cdbf9a5bad48a2024bbc2fc1bbb5f0" :answer/id #uuid "e3b1cd78-6a23-5b92-aa57-b6fe312dc7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18{t}^{2}-9t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900/selection/c3c2f096690e6e0e11eb9f1580a7297f86505759d1bf3d4fdf3b17faed2382f5" :answer/id #uuid "4d02d2e4-8d88-5c7c-996a-11078f007106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{t}^{2}+6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "efaf7af2-7a96-562f-b508-266989de8149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138900/selection/6cd854ef01bc12a8d9afee61c004093a65cdbf9a5bad48a2024bbc2fc1bbb5f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-138900/selection/0e60425cd3a5ff39671f252f602bfefa18c9c7a468398112ec2fa0ffa1233932" "q-138900/selection/83f429aa058db522ffedd829be8affa7ea9b01582aac18fc5d93a2a476fd4615" "q-138900/selection/3a4cb68b6e2420440de2a5cf842cef8eda752c3a9743289f13ed7cf2875628e2" "q-138900/selection/6cd854ef01bc12a8d9afee61c004093a65cdbf9a5bad48a2024bbc2fc1bbb5f0" "q-138900/selection/c3c2f096690e6e0e11eb9f1580a7297f86505759d1bf3d4fdf3b17faed2382f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138900" :question/id #uuid "1d0e326c-9947-5e66-959d-db32e939a7f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-138900" :question/problem "A body of mass $1.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={t}^{4}-{t}^{3}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =1.5\\cdot (12{t}^{2}-6t) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-9t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138900/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138900"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-315735/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e1c128e2-f026-54cd-af03-9ccce3af6c0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315735/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "350ef28e-1c61-5ea8-aabf-a59f99fbf641" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315735/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-315735/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315735" :question/id #uuid "92d1e0da-6675-52b1-9f96-c4f5a35a7942" :question/math-academy-id "q-315735" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$  At time $t>0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$ meters.\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=2$ seconds. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the force equals\n{{field-1}} $\\text{N}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t+\\frac{4}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+\\frac{4}{t}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =2-\\frac{4}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =ma(2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F(2)|=|2|=2\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-315735/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-315735"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345388/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "6243b63f-1ae0-59f4-969d-8ac6392776d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345388/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "c7219c7c-0fa4-5cfa-b9cd-e9ff0de6076c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345388/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6f0341-1d22-5355-a867-7e6d2804bf8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345388/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-345388/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-345388/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345388" :question/id #uuid "900029e6-9ba2-594b-a9ae-e4e625382d39" :question/math-academy-id "q-345388" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=(2t-9){e}^{-2t}$ meters per second.\n\nCalculate the time ${t}_{∗}$ at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude. Do not round the answer.\n\n${t}_{∗}=$\n\n{{field-1}}  $\\text{s}$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[(2t-9){e}^{-2t}] \\\\  & =(2t-9)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-2t})+{e}^{-2t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-9) \\\\  & =(2t-9)(-2{e}^{-2t})+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =(-4t+18){e}^{-2t}+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =(-4t+20){e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4t+20){e}^{-2t} & =0 \\\\ -4t+20 & =0 \\\\ -4t & =-20 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at ${t}_{∗}=5\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345388/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "266102e7-c8ef-55c9-8fcd-c3b6962f03b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345388"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345382/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "14ca23df-bbe5-5690-ab97-8b20b52f69d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345382/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa8f5773-6736-50db-875f-9e4bcfd65929" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345382/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-345382/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345382" :question/id #uuid "313dfc6b-b12e-5461-9869-6c76347df847" :question/math-academy-id "q-345382" :question/problem "A body of mass $1\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-8t$ meters per second.\n\nCalculate the time ${t}_{∗}$ at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude. Do not round the answer.\n\n${t}_{∗}=$\n\n{{field-1}}  $\\text{s}$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-8t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 2{t}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =4 \\\\ t & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at ${t}_{∗}=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345382/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "266102e7-c8ef-55c9-8fcd-c3b6962f03b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345382"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345391/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7129fe52-04fa-55b0-88be-0ec0c69995ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345391/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e63334d-e5db-5e4a-99c3-8002e96bb33c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345391/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-345391/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345391" :question/id #uuid "ae999be0-8621-57af-ac32-991271d83e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345391" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons. At time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{6}{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+6t+12$ meters.\n\nCalculate the time ${t}_{∗}$ at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude. Do not round the answer.\n\n${t}_{∗}=$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\text{s}$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{6}{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+6t+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-6t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-6t+6) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+t-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+t-6 & =0 \\\\ (t-2)(t+3) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at ${t}_{∗}=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-345391/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "266102e7-c8ef-55c9-8fcd-c3b6962f03b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345391"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
